    "credit": "CC0 · Art Institute of Chicago",
    "story": "Two girls sit on a terrace above the river Seine, with a basket of balls of wool on their laps. The older one wears a bright red hat; the little girl in front has flowers on hers and stares straight at us. Behind the iron railing, leaves and trees blur into a haze of green and blue. In fact they were not sisters: Renoir painted them on the terrace of the same riverside restaurant where he set his Boating Party, the same summer."
